      "text": [
        " بَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) وَ أَنَا قَائِمٌ عَلَى رَأْسِهِ وَ مَعِي إِدَاوَةٌ أَوْ قَالَ كُوزٌ فَلَمَّا انْقَطَعَ شَخْبُ الْبَوْلِ قَالَ بِيَدِهِ هَكَذَا إِلَيَّ فَنَاوَلْتُهُ بِالْمَاءِ فَتَوَضَّأَ مَكَانَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Ibn Fazzal, from Ghalib Bin Usman, from Rawh Bin Abdul Raheem who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> urinated and I was standing by his<sup>asws</sup> head, and with me was a container’, or said, ‘a pitcher. So when the flow of urine stopped, he<sup>asws</sup> said (gestured) by his<sup>asws</sup> hand like this, ‘To me<sup>asws</sup>’. So I gave it to him<sup>asws</sup> with the water, and he<sup>asws</sup> performed Ablution <span class=\"iTxt\">(Wudhu)</span> in his<sup>asws</sup> place’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Husayn from ibn Faddal from Ghalib ibn ‘Uthman from Rawh ibn ‘Abd al- Rahim who has said the following: “Once, abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, urinated. I was standing nearby with a water container or a jug. When the jet of urine stopped, he (the Imam) made a gesture with his hand for water and I gave it to him and he (the Imam) made Wudu’ at the same place.” "
        ]
      }
    },
